msgid "text/x-gmeow-patch media type"
msgstr "text/x-gmeow-patch 媒体类型"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/media-types/text/x-gmeow-patch|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The unregistered text/x-gmeow-patch MIME media type for GMEOW email-state patch or diff artifacts. Its GMEOW identity does not assert IANA registration or a universal patch-language semantics."
msgstr "用于 GMEOW 邮件状态补丁或差异制品的未注册 MIME 媒体类型 text/x-gmeow-patch。其 GMEOW 身份不表示 IANA 注册状态或通用补丁语言语义。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/media-types/text/x-gmeow-patch|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a carrier explicitly has this media format."
msgstr "用于载体明确具有此媒体格式时。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/media-types/text/x-gmeow-patch|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid using this format identity for charset, language, MIME parameters or a claim that bytes were inspected."
msgstr "避免将此格式身份用于字符集、语言、MIME 参数或声称已经检查字节。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/media-types/text/x-gmeow-patch|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Point from the carrier through mediaType to <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/media-types/text/x-gmeow-patch> and retain the exact text/x-gmeow-patch code on this value's mediaTypeName."
msgstr "通过 mediaType 从载体指向 <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/media-types/text/x-gmeow-patch>，并在该值的 mediaTypeName 上保留精确代码 text/x-gmeow-patch。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/media-types/text/x-gmeow-patch|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This is a GMEOW-owned unregistered media identity. Parameters remain outside the IRI and its MIME name; the resource does not introduce a parser."
msgstr "这是 GMEOW 拥有的未注册媒体身份。参数不属于 IRI 或其 MIME 名称；该资源不引入解析器。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/media-types/text/x-gmeow-patch|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Use this format identity: ex:file gmeow:mediaType <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/media-types/text/x-gmeow-patch> ."
msgstr "使用此格式身份：ex:file gmeow:mediaType <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/media-types/text/x-gmeow-patch> ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeIriConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Media type IRI constraint"
msgstr "媒体类型 IRI 约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeIriConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A supplied mediaType value is an IRI in the IANA registered-resource namespace or the GMEOW unregistered media-types namespace, with a type/subtype path and no parameter, query or fragment."
msgstr "已提供的 mediaType 值是 IANA 已注册资源命名空间或 GMEOW 未注册 media-types 命名空间中的 IRI，具有类型/子类型路径，且不含参数、查询或片段。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeIriConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to constrain a supplied media identity or MIME name without requiring a value on every carrier."
msgstr "用于约束已提供的媒体身份或 MIME 名称，不要求每个载体都提供值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeIriConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating a syntax check as proof of registration, correct bytes, name-to-IRI agreement or successful parsing."
msgstr "避免将语法检查视为注册状态、字节正确性、名称与 IRI 一致性或解析成功的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeIriConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Validate the supplied value using this canonical formula; registry status and exact identity selection remain explicit authored facts."
msgstr "使用此规范公式验证已提供的值；注册状态和精确身份选择仍是明确编写的事实。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeIriConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This law checks syntax only. Regex behavior is projection-dialect dependent; no registry service, MIME parser or automatic normalization is implemented by this source declaration."
msgstr "此法则仅检查语法。正则表达式行为取决于投影方言；此来源声明不实现注册表服务、MIME 解析器或自动规范化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeIriConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Use the canonical law: gmeow:MediaTypeIriConstraint logic:formalizes gmeow:mediaType ."
msgstr "使用规范法则：gmeow:MediaTypeIriConstraint logic:formalizes gmeow:mediaType ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeIriConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/message"
msgid "A supplied mediaType value is an IRI in the IANA registered-resource namespace or the GMEOW unregistered media-types namespace, with a type/subtype path and no parameter, query or fragment."
msgstr "已提供的 mediaType 值是 IANA 已注册资源命名空间或 GMEOW 未注册 media-types 命名空间中的 IRI，具有类型/子类型路径，且不含参数、查询或片段。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeNameSyntaxConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Media type name syntax constraint"
msgstr "媒体类型名称语法约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeNameSyntaxConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A supplied mediaTypeName is a parameter-free type/subtype machine spelling. Charset, whitespace and other MIME parameters do not become part of media identity."
msgstr "已提供的 mediaTypeName 是不含参数的类型/子类型机器拼写。字符集、空白及其他 MIME 参数不属于媒体身份。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeNameSyntaxConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to constrain a supplied media identity or MIME name without requiring a value on every carrier."
msgstr "用于约束已提供的媒体身份或 MIME 名称，不要求每个载体都提供值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeNameSyntaxConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid treating a syntax check as proof of registration, correct bytes, name-to-IRI agreement or successful parsing."
msgstr "避免将语法检查视为注册状态、字节正确性、名称与 IRI 一致性或解析成功的证明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeNameSyntaxConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Validate the supplied value using this canonical formula; registry status and exact identity selection remain explicit authored facts."
msgstr "使用此规范公式验证已提供的值；注册状态和精确身份选择仍是明确编写的事实。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeNameSyntaxConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This law checks syntax only. Regex behavior is projection-dialect dependent; no registry service, MIME parser or automatic normalization is implemented by this source declaration."
msgstr "此法则仅检查语法。正则表达式行为取决于投影方言；此来源声明不实现注册表服务、MIME 解析器或自动规范化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeNameSyntaxConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Use the canonical law: gmeow:MediaTypeNameSyntaxConstraint logic:formalizes gmeow:mediaTypeName ."
msgstr "使用规范法则：gmeow:MediaTypeNameSyntaxConstraint logic:formalizes gmeow:mediaTypeName ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaTypeNameSyntaxConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/message"
msgid "A supplied mediaTypeName is a parameter-free type/subtype machine spelling. Charset, whitespace and other MIME parameters do not become part of media identity."
msgstr "已提供的 mediaTypeName 是不含参数的类型/子类型机器拼写。字符集、空白及其他 MIME 参数不属于媒体身份。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/MediaObject|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Identify the image's registered format: ex:photo a gmeow:MediaObject ; gmeow:mediaType <https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/image/avif> ; gmeow:pixelWidth 4032 ; gmeow:depicts ex:lillith ."
msgstr "标识图像的已注册格式：ex:photo a gmeow:MediaObject ; gmeow:mediaType <https://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/image/avif> ; gmeow:pixelWidth 4032 ; gmeow:depicts ex:lillith ."

# Source-faithful conversation records.

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/acquiredAt|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "media acquired at"
msgstr "媒体获取时间"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/acquiredAt|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The source-supplied dateTime at which a media artifact was acquired. Acquisition is distinct from capture, publication, message sending and provider time text; missing precision or timezone is never invented."
msgstr "来源提供的媒体制品获取 dateTime。获取不同于拍摄、发布、消息发送或提供方时间文本；不得虚构缺失的精度或时区。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/acquiredAt|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the source explicitly supplies this record or field."
msgstr "用于来源明确提供此记录或字段时。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/acquiredAt|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring identity, delivery, verification or execution from missing source evidence."
msgstr "避免根据缺失的来源证据推断身份、交付、验证或执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/acquiredAt|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain exact source values, their scope and attribution; preserve supplied language and base direction."
msgstr "保留精确来源值、范围和归属，并保持所提供的语言和基本方向。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/acquiredAt|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Independent source claims coexist. These declarations preserve evidence without authenticating the provider or executing its operation."
msgstr "独立的来源主张可以并存。这些声明保留证据，不认证提供方，也不执行其操作。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/acquiredAt|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Retain the supplied value for gmeow:acquiredAt."
msgstr "保留 gmeow:acquiredAt 的来源值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalFilename|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "original media filename"
msgstr "原始媒体文件名"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalFilename|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The media artifact's original filename exactly as supplied, including case, spaces and path-like characters. It is not the email-attachment filename field, a normalized storage path or a newly resolved location."
msgstr "精确保留来源提供的媒体制品原始文件名，包括大小写、空白及类似路径的字符。它不是电子邮件附件文件名字段、规范化存储路径或新解析的位置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalFilename|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the source explicitly supplies this record or field."
msgstr "用于来源明确提供此记录或字段时。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalFilename|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring identity, delivery, verification or execution from missing source evidence."
msgstr "避免根据缺失的来源证据推断身份、交付、验证或执行。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalFilename|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain exact source values, their scope and attribution; preserve supplied language and base direction."
msgstr "保留精确来源值、范围和归属，并保持所提供的语言和基本方向。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalFilename|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Independent source claims coexist. These declarations preserve evidence without authenticating the provider or executing its operation."
msgstr "独立的来源主张可以并存。这些声明保留证据，不认证提供方，也不执行其操作。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalFilename|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Retain the supplied value for gmeow:originalFilename."
msgstr "保留 gmeow:originalFilename 的来源值。"

# Source-faithful environment interactions and catalog records.

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/channelLayout|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "channel layout as recorded"
msgstr "所记录通道布局"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/channelLayout|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The exact source string naming an image's channel layout, such as RGBA, distinct from its colour space."
msgstr "来源精确字符串，指明图像通道布局（例如 RGBA），区别于色彩空间。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/channelLayout|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an actual MediaObject has a source-supplied channel-layout code."
msgstr "用于实际 MediaObject 具有来源提供的通道布局代码时。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/channelLayout|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid token whitespace collapse, inferred colour profiles or claims of verified decoded pixels."
msgstr "避免 token 空白折叠、推断色彩配置或声称已验证解码像素。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/channelLayout|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep exact case, spaces and spelling in xsd:string or xsd:token on the media artifact."
msgstr "在媒体制品上以 xsd:string 或 xsd:token 保留精确大小写、空格和拼写。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/channelLayout|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "No parser, channel-count computation or closed code enumeration is supplied."
msgstr "不提供解析器、通道数计算或封闭代码枚举。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/channelLayout|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "For example: ex:image a gmeow:MediaObject ; gmeow:channelLayout \"RGBA\" ."
msgstr "例如：ex:image a gmeow:MediaObject ; gmeow:channelLayout \"RGBA\" ."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/identifier|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A formal external identifier of a creative work, such as a DOI or patent number, retained as the supplied xsd:string or xsd:token literal. Its scheme and spelling remain unchanged; a work may carry several identifiers."
msgstr "创作作品的正式外部标识符，如 DOI 或专利号，按所提供的 xsd:string 或 xsd:token 字面量保留。其方案和拼写不变；作品可以具有多个标识符。"


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ContentMode|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Content Mode"
msgstr "内容模式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ContentMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "An open category of values describing how the content of a source block is expressed, independently of its structural segment type."
msgstr "描述来源块内容表达方式的开放值类别，独立于其结构性片段类型。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ContentMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Prose, verse, dialogue and code are initial values, not an exhaustive inventory or mutually exclusive classes. Content mode is separate from structural kind, media format, language, genre and analysis status."
msgstr "散文、诗体、对话和代码是初始值，并非穷尽清单或互斥的类。内容模式不同于结构类别、媒体格式、语言、体裁和分析状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ContentMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Record a supplied mode: ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeVerse ."
msgstr "记录所提供的模式：ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeVerse ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ContentMode|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use as the value category for an explicitly supplied content-mode classification of a ContentBlock."
msgstr "用作 ContentBlock 已明确提供的内容模式分类的值类别。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ContentMode|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid creating a ContentBlock subclass for each mode, closing the value set or equating mode with structural segmentType or a language analysis result."
msgstr "避免为每种模式创建 ContentBlock 子类、封闭值集合，或将模式等同于结构性 segmentType 或语言分析结果。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/ContentMode|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Represent each mode as an individual of ContentMode and link the actual block through contentMode. Retain actual source and viewpoint on the exact statements and preserve other supplied modes."
msgstr "将每种模式表示为 ContentMode 的个体，并通过 contentMode 关联实际的块。在确切断言上保留实际来源和视角，并保留其他已提供的模式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentMode|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "content mode"
msgstr "内容模式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A supplied mode describing how this ContentBlock's content is expressed, separately from the block's structural segmentType."
msgstr "所提供的模式，用于描述此 ContentBlock 内容的表达方式，与该块的结构性 segmentType 分开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This optional, nonfunctional relation permits coexisting attributed classifications and mixed content. It supplies no default, exclusive winner, structural boundary or classification of every internal fragment."
msgstr "此关系可省略且非函数式，允许有归属的分类共存，并允许混合内容。它不提供默认值、唯一优先值、结构边界或对每个内部片段的分类。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentMode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "With the actual attribution retained, record ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeDialogue, gmeow:contentModeVerse ."
msgstr "保留实际归属，并记录 ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeDialogue, gmeow:contentModeVerse ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentMode|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a source or attributed analysis supplies a content mode for the block actually being described."
msgstr "当来源或有归属的分析为实际描述的块提供内容模式时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentMode|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid substituting mode for structural kind or inferring a mode solely from layout, markup, a missing value or another mode."
msgstr "避免用模式替代结构类别，或仅根据版式、标记、缺失值或另一种模式推断模式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentMode|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the ContentBlock to each supplied ContentMode individual. Retain its existing segmentType and exact-statement attribution without requiring a mode on every block or selecting one preferred value."
msgstr "将 ContentBlock 关联到每个已提供的 ContentMode 个体。保留其现有 segmentType 和确切断言的归属，不要求每个块都有模式，也不选择一个首选值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeProse|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "prose content mode"
msgstr "散文内容模式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeProse|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content mode for a block presented as prose, without imposing a paragraph shape or language-analysis status."
msgstr "用于呈现为散文的块的内容模式，不强加段落形态或语言分析状态。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeProse|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "A prose classification does not establish a paragraph boundary, a particular language or an unanalyzed surface. Other supplied modes may coexist on the same block."
msgstr "散文分类不确立段落边界、特定语言或未经分析的表层形式。同一块上可以共存其他已提供的模式。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeProse|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Record supplied prose classification: ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeProse ."
msgstr "记录所提供的散文分类：ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeProse ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeProse|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the selected block's content is explicitly presented or classified as prose."
msgstr "当所选块的内容明确呈现为散文或被归类为散文时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeProse|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid assigning prose by default to an unclassified block or treating it as lang:UnanalyzedProse or lang:renderingProse."
msgstr "避免默认将未分类的块归为散文，或将其视为 lang:UnanalyzedProse 或 lang:renderingProse。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeProse|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reference this value through contentMode on the actual ContentBlock and retain the supplied classification's source and viewpoint. Keep structural and analysis-status assertions separate."
msgstr "在实际的 ContentBlock 上通过 contentMode 引用此值，并保留所提供分类的来源和视角。将结构断言与分析状态断言分开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeVerse|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "verse content mode"
msgstr "诗体内容模式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeVerse|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content mode for content presented as verse, independently of the block's structural boundaries."
msgstr "用于呈现为诗体的内容的内容模式，独立于块的结构边界。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeVerse|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This value does not require a line or stanza boundary, rhyme, meter or a parsed poetic structure. Verse may coexist with a supplied dialogue or other mode classification."
msgstr "此值不要求诗行或诗节边界、押韵、格律或已解析的诗歌结构。诗体可以与已提供的对话或其他模式分类共存。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeVerse|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Record supplied verse classification: ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeVerse ."
msgstr "记录所提供的诗体分类：ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeVerse ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeVerse|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the selected block's content is explicitly presented or classified as verse."
msgstr "当所选块的内容明确呈现为诗体或被归类为诗体时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeVerse|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid deriving verse from typography alone or replacing segmentTypeVerse, whose role is structural."
msgstr "避免仅根据排版推断诗体，或替代承担结构角色的 segmentTypeVerse。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeVerse|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reference this value through contentMode and retain the actual attribution. Preserve any independently supplied structural segment type and other modes without imposing metrical or boundary rules."
msgstr "通过 contentMode 引用此值并保留实际归属。保留任何独立提供的结构性片段类型和其他模式，不强加格律或边界规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeDialogue|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "dialogue content mode"
msgstr "对话内容模式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeDialogue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content mode for content presented as dialogue, independently of structural segmentation and speaker attribution."
msgstr "用于呈现为对话的内容的内容模式，独立于结构分段和说话者归属。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeDialogue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Dialogue classification supplies no actual speaker, turn count, fictional or real participant identity, or occurrence of a real conversation. It may coexist with prose or verse classification."
msgstr "对话分类不提供实际说话者、轮次数、虚构或真实参与者身份，也不确立真实会话的发生。它可以与散文或诗体分类共存。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeDialogue|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Record supplied dialogue classification: ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeDialogue ."
msgstr "记录所提供的对话分类：ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeDialogue ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeDialogue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the selected block's content is explicitly presented or classified as dialogue."
msgstr "当所选块的内容明确呈现为对话或被归类为对话时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeDialogue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid manufacturing a speaker, conversation event or turn structure, or substituting this value for structural segmentTypeDialogue."
msgstr "避免虚构说话者、会话事件或轮次结构，或用此值替代结构性的 segmentTypeDialogue。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeDialogue|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reference this value through contentMode and retain the actual classification's source and viewpoint. Record independently supplied speaker and structural information through their existing properties."
msgstr "通过 contentMode 引用此值，并保留实际分类的来源和视角。通过现有属性记录独立提供的说话者信息和结构信息。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeCode|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "code content mode"
msgstr "代码内容模式"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeCode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The content mode for content presented as code, independently of the block's structural layout or programming-language attribution."
msgstr "用于呈现为代码的内容的内容模式，独立于块的结构布局或编程语言归属。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeCode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This value supplies no programming-language identity, syntactic validity, execution, successful result or security judgment. Code classification may coexist with other supplied modes."
msgstr "此值不提供编程语言身份、语法有效性、执行、成功结果或安全判断。代码分类可以与其他已提供的模式共存。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeCode|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Record supplied code classification: ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeCode ."
msgstr "记录所提供的代码分类：ex:block gmeow:contentMode gmeow:contentModeCode ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeCode|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the selected block's content is explicitly presented or classified as code."
msgstr "当所选块的内容明确呈现为代码或被归类为代码时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeCode|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid executing the content or inferring a programming language, validity or safety from this value, or substituting it for structural segmentTypeCodeListing."
msgstr "避免执行该内容，或根据此值推断编程语言、有效性或安全性，或用它替代结构性的 segmentTypeCodeListing。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/contentModeCode|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Reference this value through contentMode and retain the actual attribution. Keep the independently supplied structural kind and programming-language wording separate."
msgstr "通过 contentMode 引用此值并保留实际归属。将独立提供的结构类别与编程语言表述分开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/headingLevel|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "source heading level"
msgstr "源标题层级"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/headingLevel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The integer reported by a source or attributed analysis as the heading-level code for this ContentBlock."
msgstr "源或有明确归属的分析所报告的整数，用作此 ContentBlock 的标题层级代码。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/headingLevel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Interpret this reported code only under the actual source convention. It supplies no universal level origin, bound or ordering, computed containment depth or segment position. Distinct attributed readings may coexist."
msgstr "仅依据源的实际约定解释此报告的代码。它不提供通用的层级起点、界限或排序，也不提供计算所得的包含深度或分段位置。具有各自归属的不同解读可以并存。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/headingLevel|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Retain a supplied level: ex:heading gmeow:headingLevel 2 . Preserve the actual source convention and statement attribution when supplied."
msgstr "保留提供的层级：ex:heading gmeow:headingLevel 2 . 若提供了源的实际约定和陈述归属，也应一并保留。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/headingLevel|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to preserve an explicit integer heading level supplied for the source block being described."
msgstr "用于保留为所描述的源块明确提供的整数标题层级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/headingLevel|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inventing a level from typography, segmentIndex, printedLabel or containment, assuming an unreported numbering convention, or converting an unknown code into a globally comparable rank."
msgstr "避免根据排版、segmentIndex、printedLabel 或包含关系编造层级，假定未报告的编号约定，或将未知代码转换为可全局比较的等级。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/headingLevel|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep the supplied xsd:integer on the actual ContentBlock with its existing segmentType. Retain source, viewpoint and any supplied convention on the exact assertion; keep missing context unknown without selecting a preferred level or changing other readings."
msgstr "将提供的 xsd:integer 保留在实际的 ContentBlock 上，并保留其现有 segmentType。在确切的断言上保留源、视点及任何已提供的约定；缺失的上下文应保持未知，不选择优先层级，也不改变其他解读。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalMediaTypeText|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "reported original media-format text"
msgstr "报告的原始媒体格式文本"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalMediaTypeText|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The exact source string reporting a pre-reencoding media format associated with this actual stored MediaObject."
msgstr "报告与此实际存储 MediaObject 相关的重新编码前媒体格式的原样来源字符串。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalMediaTypeText|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This optional, nonfunctional machine string preserves an attributed history claim, not an original asset or validated MIME identity. Different original-format claims can coexist on the same held carrier."
msgstr "此机器字符串可省略且不具有函数性，保留具有归属信息的历史声明，不表示原始资产或已验证的 MIME 身份。同一保存载体上可以并存不同的原始格式声明。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalMediaTypeText|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A fictional source retains `ex:image gmeow:originalMediaTypeText \" JPEG \" .` without trimming the spaces."
msgstr "一个虚构来源保留 `ex:image gmeow:originalMediaTypeText \" JPEG \" .`，不裁去空格。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalMediaTypeText|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when a source supplies original pre-reencoding format text for an actual stored media artifact."
msgstr "当来源为实际存储的媒体对象提供重新编码前的原始格式文本时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalMediaTypeText|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid replacing the held carrier’s mediaType, inventing an original asset, normalizing MIME syntax or selecting one source history as universal."
msgstr "避免替换保存载体的 mediaType、编造原始资产、规范化 MIME 语法，或将某个来源历史选为普遍事实。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/originalMediaTypeText|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep every supplied xsd:string exactly, including case, spaces and blank text, with its actual exact-statement source and any supplied viewpoint. Leave unavailable text absent."
msgstr "原样保留每个已提供的 xsd:string，包括大小写、空格和空文本，并保留精确陈述的实际来源及任何已提供视角。未提供文本时省略。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubSpineEntry|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "EPUB spine-entry account"
msgstr "EPUB spine 条目记录"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubSpineEntry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A source-supplied information-record account of one EPUB spine entry, retaining its reported order descriptor, exact href and any supplied ordered TOC path."
msgstr "由来源提供的单个 EPUB spine 条目信息记录，保留报告的顺序描述值、精确 href 以及任何已提供的有序目录路径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubSpineEntry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Each coherent account requires one reported integer order descriptor and one href string. Its path and actual source association are optional; matching descriptors or hrefs do not merge accounts or establish parsed EPUB conformance."
msgstr "每个一致记录要求一个报告的整数顺序描述值和一个 href 字符串。路径及实际来源关联均可选；相同描述值或 href 不会合并记录，也不确立已解析 EPUB 的符合性。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubSpineEntry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A fictional source supplies two distinct entry accounts with the same relative href while preserving their separate order descriptors and attribution."
msgstr "一个虚构来源提供两个具有相同相对 href 的不同条目记录，同时保留各自的顺序描述值和归属。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubSpineEntry|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain a coherent source-supplied EPUB spine-entry record without resolving its href or reconstructing its source package."
msgstr "用于保留由来源提供的一致 EPUB spine 条目记录，不解析其 href，也不重建其源包。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubSpineEntry|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring a package identity, base URI, immutable revision, digest, parser success, resolved content target or universal ordering convention from the record alone."
msgstr "避免仅凭记录推断包身份、基础 URI、不可变修订版、摘要、解析成功、已解析内容目标或通用顺序约定。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubSpineEntry|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep each supplied account distinct. Retain epubSpineOrder and epubSpineHref, add epubTocPath only when supplied, and associate an actually identified source through epubSpineEntry without inventing missing context."
msgstr "保持每个已提供记录独立。保留 epubSpineOrder 和 epubSpineHref，仅在提供时添加 epubTocPath，并通过 epubSpineEntry 关联实际已识别来源，不虚构缺失语境。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathStep|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "EPUB TOC path step"
msgstr "EPUB 目录路径步骤"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathStep|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A StructuredValue occurrence representing one supplied EPUB TOC path step, whose sole scalar structuredTerm is its complete title and whose epubTocDepth retains the reported depth descriptor."
msgstr "一种 StructuredValue 出现项，表示一个已提供的 EPUB 目录路径步骤；其唯一标量 structuredTerm 是完整标题，epubTocDepth 保留报告的深度描述值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathStep|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Every typed step requires its title and reported integer depth, even before path membership is supplied. Title identity is the complete RDF term; equal titles on distinct occurrences do not identify the same step."
msgstr "每个已声明类型的步骤都要求标题和报告的整数深度，即使尚未提供路径成员关系。标题身份取决于完整 RDF 项；不同出现项上的相同标题不确立同一步骤。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathStep|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Two distinct path steps retain the same spaced title at different entryOrdinal positions; a standalone typed step still supplies its own title and depth."
msgstr "两个不同路径步骤在不同 entryOrdinal 位置保留同一含空格标题；独立的已声明类型步骤仍须提供其自身标题和深度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathStep|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for an actual supplied TOC step occurrence with a complete word-literal title and its reported depth descriptor."
msgstr "当提供实际目录步骤出现项、完整文字字面量标题及报告的深度描述值时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathStep|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid adding a duplicate title field or wrapper identity, deriving depth from entryOrdinal, inferring a tree or replacing repeated or blank titles with missing data."
msgstr "避免添加重复标题字段或包装身份，避免从 entryOrdinal 推导深度、推断树结构，或把重复标题及空标题替换为缺失数据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathStep|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Type the actual occurrence EpubTocPathStep, retain its complete title once through structuredTerm and its supplied integer depth through epubTocDepth. When it belongs to a path, retain its actual zero-based occurrence position through entryOrdinal."
msgstr "将实际出现项声明为 EpubTocPathStep，通过 structuredTerm 仅保留一次完整标题，并通过 epubTocDepth 保留已提供的整数深度。当其属于路径时，通过 entryOrdinal 保留实际从零开始的出现位置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineEntry|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "reported EPUB spine-entry account"
msgstr "报告的 EPUB spine 条目记录关联"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineEntry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Relates an actually identified source InformationObject to an EpubSpineEntry account supplied for that source."
msgstr "将实际已识别的源 InformationObject 关联到为该来源提供的 EpubSpineEntry 记录。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineEntry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This optional, nonfunctional association retains supplied source context without identifying an immutable revision, declaring a media type or proving completeness of a package inventory. A source may have independent accounts."
msgstr "此可选且非函数性的关联保留已提供来源语境，不识别不可变修订版、不声明媒体类型，也不证明包清单完整。一个来源可具有多个独立记录。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineEntry|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A fictional source links to two independently attributed entry accounts; another supplied entry remains unassociated when its actual source identity is unavailable."
msgstr "一个虚构来源关联到两个各自记录归属的条目记录；另一个已提供条目在实际来源身份不可获取时不建立来源关联。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineEntry|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the actual source information object and its supplied spine-entry account are identified."
msgstr "当实际源信息对象及为其提供的 spine 条目记录均已识别时使用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineEntry|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid minting a source to fill missing evidence or substituting segmentOf, wasDerivedFrom or navigationSource for this supplied account association."
msgstr "避免创建来源以填补证据缺失，也避免用 segmentOf、wasDerivedFrom 或 navigationSource 代替此已提供记录关联。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineEntry|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link only an actual supplied InformationObject to each distinct entry account and attribute the association itself. Leave unavailable source identity absent; shared href wording does not create this link."
msgstr "仅将实际已提供的 InformationObject 关联到各个不同条目记录，并记录该关联本身的归属。来源身份不可获取时保持缺失；相同 href 措辞不会生成此关联。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineOrder|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "reported EPUB spine order descriptor"
msgstr "报告的 EPUB spine 顺序描述值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineOrder|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The integer descriptor supplied by the source for the order of this EPUB spine-entry account under its actual convention."
msgstr "来源按其实际约定为此 EPUB spine 条目记录的顺序提供的整数描述值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineOrder|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Exactly one integer-family literal is required per account. Its supplied lexical form and datatype survive; no universal origin, bound, tie policy, comparison rule or canonical sequence position is established."
msgstr "每个记录要求恰好一个整数族字面量。保留已提供词法形式和数据类型；不确立通用起点、边界、并列规则、比较规则或规范序列位置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineOrder|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A source supplies order descriptor 12 while the first TOC step has entryOrdinal 0; the two integers describe different things."
msgstr "来源提供顺序描述值 12，而首个目录步骤的 entryOrdinal 为 0；两个整数描述不同事项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineOrder|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain the supplied integer spine-order descriptor independently of TOC depth and actual step position."
msgstr "用于独立保留已提供的整数 spine 顺序描述值，使其与目录深度及实际步骤位置分开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineOrder|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid copying this descriptor into entryOrdinal, inventing a numbering base or coercing a string, fractional value or arbitrary code into interpreted spine order."
msgstr "避免把此描述值复制到 entryOrdinal、虚构编号基准，或将字符串、分数值及任意代码强制解释为 spine 顺序。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineOrder|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep the exact supplied literal from the thirteen XSD integer-family datatypes, with its source convention and exact-statement attribution. Invalid selected input fails rather than being normalized or replaced."
msgstr "保留来自十三种 XSD 整数族数据类型的精确已提供字面量，以及来源约定和精确陈述归属。选定输入无效时应失败，不做规范化或替换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineHref|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "reported EPUB spine href"
msgstr "报告的 EPUB spine href"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineHref|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The exact href string supplied by the source for this EPUB spine-entry account, retained without URI resolution or normalization."
msgstr "来源为此 EPUB spine 条目记录提供的精确 href 字符串，保留时不进行 URI 解析或规范化。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineHref|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Exactly one xsd:string is required, including a supplied blank string. Relative spelling, case, spaces and fragments remain source data; the string establishes no independent content-resource identity or base URI."
msgstr "要求恰好一个 xsd:string，包括已提供的空字符串。相对拼写、大小写、空格和片段均保持为源数据；字符串不确立独立内容资源身份或基础 URI。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineHref|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A fictional source retains Text/Part.xhtml#Opening exactly as its relative href, without guessing a package location."
msgstr "一个虚构来源将 Text/Part.xhtml#Opening 原样保留为相对 href，不猜测包位置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineHref|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the entry account supplies its exact href field, including relative or blank text."
msgstr "当条目记录提供其精确 href 字段时使用，包括相对文本或空文本。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineHref|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid resolving or fetching the reference, decoding or rewriting its spelling, adding a language tag or treating matching strings as target identity."
msgstr "避免解析或获取该引用、解码或改写其拼写、添加语言标签，或把相同字符串当作目标身份。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubSpineHref|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the complete supplied xsd:string with its exact-statement source and viewpoint. Any separately supplied resolved target or base context remains distinct evidence, not a computed value of this property."
msgstr "保留完整已提供 xsd:string，以及精确陈述的来源和视角。另行提供的已解析目标或基础语境属于独立证据，不是此属性的计算值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocPath|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "reported EPUB TOC path"
msgstr "报告的 EPUB 目录路径"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocPath|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The independently ordered StructuredSequence of TOC path-step occurrences supplied for this EPUB spine-entry account."
msgstr "为此 EPUB spine 条目记录提供的目录路径步骤出现项所组成的独立有序 StructuredSequence。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocPath|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This optional path is locally at most one. An actually supplied current empty sequence differs from absence; code defaults do not recover historical field presence. The path establishes no inferred navigation tree or resolved targets."
msgstr "此可选路径局部至多一个。实际提供的当前空序列不同于缺失；代码默认值不能恢复历史字段是否存在。该路径不确立推断出的导航树或已解析目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocPath|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "One account supplies an empty TOC path while another supplies no path; a third preserves equal titles as separate ordered step occurrences."
msgstr "一个记录提供空目录路径，另一个记录未提供路径；第三个记录把相同标题保留为不同的有序步骤出现项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocPath|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the entry account actually supplies its ordered TOC path, including a known current zero-item path."
msgstr "当条目记录实际提供其有序目录路径时使用，包括已知当前零项路径。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocPath|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inventing a path for a missing field, removing repeated or blank titles, pairing positions across accounts or deriving parent-child relations from depth descriptors."
msgstr "避免为缺失字段虚构路径、删除重复或空标题、跨记录配对位置，或从深度描述值推导父子关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocPath|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link one supplied StructuredSequence whose items are distinct EpubTocPathStep occurrences. Retain their actual zero-based positions with entryOrdinal and preserve each complete title and supplied depth under its own source attribution."
msgstr "关联一个已提供的 StructuredSequence，其各项为不同 EpubTocPathStep 出现项。使用 entryOrdinal 保留实际从零开始的位置，并分别按其来源归属保留完整标题和已提供深度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocDepth|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "reported EPUB TOC depth descriptor"
msgstr "报告的 EPUB 目录深度描述值"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocDepth|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The integer descriptor supplied by the source as the depth of this EPUB TOC path step under its actual convention."
msgstr "来源按其实际约定作为此 EPUB 目录路径步骤深度提供的整数描述值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocDepth|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Exactly one integer-family literal is required per typed step. It is a reported descriptor, not a computed count, canonical tree depth or occurrence position; its actual source convention governs interpretation."
msgstr "每个已声明类型步骤要求恰好一个整数族字面量。它是报告的描述值，不是计算出的计数、规范树深度或出现位置；应按实际来源约定解释。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocDepth|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "The first path step retains reported depth 4 at entryOrdinal 0 without inferring four ancestors or a missing prefix."
msgstr "首个路径步骤在 entryOrdinal 为 0 时保留报告的深度 4，不推断四个祖先或缺失前缀。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocDepth|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the actual integer depth descriptor supplied with a TOC step, independently of path position and spine order."
msgstr "用于保留随目录步骤实际提供的整数深度描述值，使其与路径位置及 spine 顺序分开。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocDepth|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid computing depth from path length, imposing an unreported origin or bound, copying it into entryOrdinal or accepting an arbitrary integer code as interpreted depth."
msgstr "避免从路径长度计算深度、施加未报告起点或边界、将其复制到 entryOrdinal，或把任意整数代码接受为已解释深度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/epubTocDepth|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Retain the exact supplied integer-family literal and its actual source convention on this occurrence. Preserve lexical form and datatype; invalid or noninteger selected input fails without coercion or a synthesized default."
msgstr "在此出现项上保留精确已提供整数族字面量及实际来源约定。保留词法形式和数据类型；选定输入无效或非整数时应失败，不做强制转换，也不生成默认值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathItemConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "EPUB TOC path-item constraint"
msgstr "EPUB 目录路径项约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathItemConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Every structuredItem in a sequence selected through epubTocPath is an EpubTocPathStep occurrence."
msgstr "通过 epubTocPath 选取的序列中，每个 structuredItem 都是 EpubTocPathStep 出现项。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathItemConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This role-scoped law checks every selected item without requiring an explicitly typed entry. Empty selected paths remain valid; generic sequence branch and ordinal contracts remain unchanged."
msgstr "此按角色限定的规则检查每个选中项，不要求条目显式声明类型。选中的空路径仍有效；通用序列分支及序号契约保持不变。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathItemConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A selected path item typed only as a generic StructuredValue does not bypass the EpubTocPathStep title and depth contract."
msgstr "选中的路径项即使仅声明为通用 StructuredValue，也不能绕过 EpubTocPathStep 的标题和深度契约。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathItemConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to enforce the step-occurrence contract on every supplied TOC path item without narrowing unrelated generic sequences."
msgstr "用于将步骤出现项契约应用于每个已提供目录路径项，不收窄无关通用序列。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathItemConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid accepting one well-formed step as cover for another malformed item or interpreting a scalar title string as a resolved navigation resource."
msgstr "避免用一个合规步骤掩盖另一个不合规项，也避免把标量标题字符串解释为已解析导航资源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathItemConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Follow epubTocPath and every structuredItem, requiring EpubTocPathStep membership for each item. Preserve its distinct occurrence, actual title, depth and canonical sequence position without inventing a target."
msgstr "沿 epubTocPath 和每个 structuredItem 检查，要求各项属于 EpubTocPathStep。保留其不同出现项、实际标题、深度及规范序列位置，不虚构目标。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathTitleConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "EPUB TOC step-title constraint"
msgstr "EPUB 目录步骤标题约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathTitleConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Every typed EpubTocPathStep has a scalar structuredTerm title, and every supplied title term is an xsd:string, rdf:langString or rdf:dirLangString literal."
msgstr "每个已声明类型的 EpubTocPathStep 都具有标量 structuredTerm 标题，且每个已提供标题项都是 xsd:string、rdf:langString 或 rdf:dirLangString 字面量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathTitleConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The title is required even for a standalone typed step. Blank titles are valid; generic StructuredValue laws still enforce one scalar branch and exact whole-term identity without a duplicate title authority."
msgstr "即使是独立的已声明类型步骤，也必须具有标题。允许空标题；通用 StructuredValue 规则仍强制要求单一标量分支和精确完整项身份，不设置重复标题权威。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathTitleConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A standalone step with a blank string title satisfies title presence; a step missing structuredTerm or carrying a numeric, resource or extra malformed term violates this law."
msgstr "独立步骤的标题为空字符串时满足标题存在要求；步骤缺少 structuredTerm，或带有数字项、资源项或额外不合规项值时，违反此规则。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathTitleConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to require and validate every supplied title on each typed TOC step, whether or not path membership is present."
msgstr "用于要求并验证每个已声明类型目录步骤上的每个已提供标题，不取决于是否存在路径成员关系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathTitleConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid accepting an empty container as a missing title, coercing nonword values into strings or allowing a good title to hide another invalid supplied term."
msgstr "避免用空容器代替缺失标题，避免把非文字值强制转换为字符串，也避免让合规标题掩盖另一个无效的已提供项值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/EpubTocPathTitleConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Require a structuredTerm on every typed step, then compare every supplied term’s datatype through termSameComponent with the three admitted word datatypes. Keep the original complete literal and reject violations without rewriting input."
msgstr "要求每个已声明类型步骤具有 structuredTerm，再通过 termSameComponent 将每个已提供项的数据类型与三个允许的文字数据类型比较。保留原始完整字面量，拒绝违规输入而不改写。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceLocus|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "source locus"
msgstr "来源位置"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceLocus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A supplied EvidenceSpan locating this documentary information object within its source, retaining its actual page, href or region context."
msgstr "来源提供的 EvidenceSpan，用于定位此文献信息对象在其来源中的位置，并保留实际的页码、href 或区域上下文。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceLocus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This optional, nonfunctional role supports ContentBlock and other documentary information objects without creating a CitationAct, retrieval Chunk or source revision. Preserve distinct supplied loci and their attribution; no missing locator becomes zero, blank or null."
msgstr "此可选且非函数式的关系适用于 ContentBlock 及其他文献信息对象，不创建 CitationAct、检索 Chunk 或来源修订版。保留不同的来源位置及其归属；缺失定位信息不变成零值、空白或空值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceLocus|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A block retains a supplied page span; a region-bearing span uses the same locus route with four framed coordinate quantities."
msgstr "块保留来源提供的页面位置；带区域的位置通过同一关系保留四个具有参考系的坐标量。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceLocus|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to retain the actual source locus supplied for documentary content."
msgstr "用于保留文献内容实际提供的来源位置。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceLocus|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid substituting viaSelector, inventing an immutable source, resolving hrefs or treating page geometry as Unicode offsets."
msgstr "避免替换为 viaSelector、编造不可变来源、解析 href，或将页面几何位置视为 Unicode 偏移。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceLocus|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the actual span, reuse selectorPage for its original page literal and locusHref for its exact href, and type that same span SourceRegion when its four coordinate quantities are supplied."
msgstr "连接实际位置，使用 selectorPage 保留原始页面字面量，使用 locusHref 保留确切 href；当提供四个坐标量时，将同一位置标为 SourceRegion。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusSource|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "locus source"
msgstr "位置所依据的来源"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusSource|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The actually identified source information artifact within which this EvidenceSpan is located."
msgstr "此 EvidenceSpan 所处的、实际已标明的信息来源制品。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusSource|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The optional role retains at most one supplied artifact per coherent span. It does not infer an immutable revision, byte identity, format or source authentication from a work name, media identifier, href or path."
msgstr "此可选关系在每个一致的位置记录中至多保留一个来源制品。它不从作品名称、媒体标识、href 或路径推断不可变修订版、字节身份、格式或来源认证。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusSource|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "An independently identified source artifact is retained separately from the span’s unresolved href wording."
msgstr "独立标明的来源制品与位置中尚未解析的 href 文本分别保留。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusSource|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when the source information artifact itself is actually identified."
msgstr "用于实际标明信息来源制品本身时。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusSource|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid creating an artifact or revision from a filename, locator, digest resemblance or abstract work identity."
msgstr "避免从文件名、定位信息、摘要相似性或抽象作品身份创建制品或修订版。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusSource|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link only the actual supplied InformationObject artifact. Preserve any genuinely supplied revision or digest separately under its existing contract; leave unavailable artifact identity absent."
msgstr "仅连接实际提供的 InformationObject 制品。按现有契约分别保留确实提供的修订版或摘要；若制品身份不可得，则保持缺失。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusHref|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "locus href"
msgstr "位置 href"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusHref|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The exact supplied textual href reference locating this EvidenceSpan within its source."
msgstr "用于定位此 EvidenceSpan 在其来源中位置的、来源所提供的确切 href 文本引用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusHref|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "This optional role retains at most one original xsd:string, xsd:token or xsd:anyURI literal per coherent span. It specializes selectorLocator without resolving a target, supplying a base URI, normalizing the literal or establishing source-file identity."
msgstr "此可选关系在每个一致的位置记录中至多保留一个原始 xsd:string、xsd:token 或 xsd:anyURI 字面量。它特化 selectorLocator，但不解析目标、不提供基准 URI、不规范化字面量，也不确立来源文件身份。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusHref|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A relative href with its supplied fragment and spacing remains source text rather than a newly resolved resource."
msgstr "相对 href 保留来源提供的片段和空白，仍是来源文本，而不是新解析出的资源。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusHref|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the actual href reference supplied with a source locus."
msgstr "用于随来源位置实际提供的 href 引用。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusHref|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid replacing the literal with an IRI object, casting between admitted datatypes, resolving a path or substituting sourceLocation."
msgstr "避免将字面量替换为 IRI 对象、在允许的数据类型之间转换、解析路径或替换为 sourceLocation。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/locusHref|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Keep the complete supplied literal on the span once. Its unchanged object follows the generic selectorLocator relation by subproperty entailment; do not author a second locator copy."
msgstr "在位置上只保留一次完整的来源字面量。其原样对象通过子属性蕴涵满足通用 selectorLocator 关系；不要再编写一个定位值副本。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegion|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Source Region"
msgstr "来源区域"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "A supplied region-bearing EvidenceSpan retaining the four source coordinate slots x0, y0, x1 and y1 as framed math:Quantity values in one actual declared coordinate frame."
msgstr "来源提供的带区域 EvidenceSpan，将来源坐标槽 x0、y0、x1 和 y1 保留为处于同一实际声明坐标参考系中的 math:Quantity 值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "The coordinate roles preserve the source’s actual interpretation, not a guessed origin, axis direction, unit, pixel grid, normalized fraction, corner inclusion or geometric inequality. The same span retains any supplied selectorPage, locusHref and independently identified locusSource."
msgstr "坐标关系保留来源的实际解释，不猜测原点、轴方向、单位、像素网格、归一化比例、边界包含关系或几何不等式。同一位置保留任何来源提供的 selectorPage、locusHref，以及独立标明的 locusSource。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegion|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A page region retains its original numeric literals and evidenced coordinate frame without converting corner slots into width and height."
msgstr "页面区域保留原始数值字面量及有依据的坐标参考系，不将角点槽转换为宽度和高度。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use when an actual source supplies all four numeric coordinate slots and their real interpretation is supported."
msgstr "用于实际来源提供全部四个数值坐标槽，且其实际解释有依据时。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid raw numeric aliases, opaque rectangle blobs, rational-vector coercion, invented frames or identifying the locus with a stored image or geographic observation."
msgstr "避免原始数值别名、不透明矩形数据块、强制有理向量转换、编造参考系，或将位置等同于已存储图像或地理观测。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegion|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Supply exactly one Quantity per coordinate role and one complete actual hasReferenceFrame on the region. Retain original finite numeric magnitudes, each Quantity’s inherited dimension and a frame agreeing with the region; preserve actual source and interpretation evidence."
msgstr "为每个坐标关系提供恰好一个 Quantity，并在区域上提供一个实际完整的 hasReferenceFrame。保留原始有限数值、每个 Quantity 继承的维度，以及与区域一致的参考系；保留实际来源及解释证据。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegionCoordinateConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "Source region coordinate constraint"
msgstr "来源区域坐标约束"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegionCoordinateConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "Every SourceRegion coordinate Quantity has an original valid finite numeric magnitude, one numeric value and an actual frame equal to the region’s required single coordinate frame."
msgstr "每个 SourceRegion 坐标 Quantity 都必须具有有效的原始有限数值、唯一的数值，以及与区域所要求的唯一坐标参考系相同的实际参考系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegionCoordinateConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Equivalent retained source lexical aliases may coexist under numeric equality. Existing Quantity dimension requirements and ReferenceFrame obligations remain authoritative. This law supplies no dimension default, coordinate conversion, source authentication or geometric bound."
msgstr "保留的等价来源词法变体可在数值相等时并存。现有 Quantity 维度要求和 ReferenceFrame 义务仍为准。此规则不提供默认维度、坐标转换、来源认证或几何界限。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegionCoordinateConstraint|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "Two source spellings of the same valid numeric value remain intact on a compatible coordinate Quantity; an invented frame never repairs missing interpretation."
msgstr "同一有效数值的两种来源拼写可在兼容的坐标 Quantity 上原样保留；编造参考系无法补足缺失的解释。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegionCoordinateConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use to validate the magnitudes and same-frame context of every supplied source-region coordinate."
msgstr "用于校验每个来源区域坐标的数值及共同参考系上下文。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegionCoordinateConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid dropping invalid coordinates, retyping values, manufacturing dimensions or frames, or adding page/axis bounds not stated by the source."
msgstr "避免丢弃无效坐标、改变数值类型、制造维度或参考系，或添加来源未声明的页面或坐标轴界限。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegionCoordinateConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Apply the outer region guard and each independent positive coordinate-role guard. Require magnitude and frame presence, finite numeric validity, numeric-value equality and agreement of every coordinate frame with the region frame."
msgstr "应用外层区域守卫及每个独立的正向坐标关系守卫。要求数值和参考系存在、有限数值有效、数值相等，以及每个坐标参考系与区域参考系一致。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/SourceRegionCoordinateConstraint|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/message"
msgid "Every SourceRegion coordinate Quantity has an original valid finite numeric magnitude, one numeric value and an actual frame equal to the region’s required single coordinate frame."
msgstr "每个 SourceRegion 坐标 Quantity 都必须具有有效的原始有限数值、唯一的数值，以及与区域所要求的唯一坐标参考系相同的实际参考系。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionX0|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "source region x0"
msgstr "来源区域 x0"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionX0|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The existing math:Quantity retaining the original numeric value supplied in the x0 coordinate slot of this SourceRegion."
msgstr "保留此 SourceRegion 的 x0 坐标槽中来源提供的原始数值的现有 math:Quantity。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionX0|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Exactly one Quantity fills this source slot. Its finite numeric literal keeps its original datatype and spelling; the role asserts no axis origin, direction, unit, sign restriction, corner convention or coordinate conversion."
msgstr "此来源槽恰好关联一个 Quantity。其有限数值字面量保持原始数据类型和拼写；此关系不声明轴原点、方向、单位、正负限制、角点约定或坐标转换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionX0|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A source’s x0 numeric term remains unchanged on its Quantity rather than being copied into a raw rectangle string."
msgstr "来源的 x0 数值项在其 Quantity 上保持不变，不复制到原始矩形字符串中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionX0|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the actual numeric value supplied for the x0 slot."
msgstr "用于来源实际提供的 x0 槽数值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionX0|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring this coordinate from another slot, replacing absence with zero or forcing a pixel, fractional or rational representation."
msgstr "避免从其他槽推断此坐标、以零补足缺失值，或强制使用像素、比例或有理数表示。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionX0|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the actual Quantity, retain its original magnitude through math:quantityValue, keep its inherited actual dimension and require its frame to agree with this region’s actual coordinate frame."
msgstr "连接实际 Quantity，通过 math:quantityValue 保留原始数值，保留其继承的实际维度，并要求其参考系与此区域实际的坐标参考系一致。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionY0|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "source region y0"
msgstr "来源区域 y0"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionY0|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The existing math:Quantity retaining the original numeric value supplied in the y0 coordinate slot of this SourceRegion."
msgstr "保留此 SourceRegion 的 y0 坐标槽中来源提供的原始数值的现有 math:Quantity。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionY0|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote"
msgid "Exactly one Quantity fills this source slot. Its finite numeric literal keeps its original datatype and spelling; the role asserts no axis origin, direction, unit, sign restriction, corner convention or coordinate conversion."
msgstr "此来源槽恰好关联一个 Quantity。其有限数值字面量保持原始数据类型和拼写；此关系不声明轴原点、方向、单位、正负限制、角点约定或坐标转换。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionY0|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example"
msgid "A source’s y0 numeric term remains unchanged on its Quantity rather than being copied into a raw rectangle string."
msgstr "来源的 y0 数值项在其 Quantity 上保持不变，不复制到原始矩形字符串中。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionY0|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/useWhen"
msgid "Use for the actual numeric value supplied for the y0 slot."
msgstr "用于来源实际提供的 y0 槽数值。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionY0|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/avoidWhen"
msgid "Avoid inferring this coordinate from another slot, replacing absence with zero or forcing a pixel, fractional or rational representation."
msgstr "避免从其他槽推断此坐标、以零补足缺失值，或强制使用像素、比例或有理数表示。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionY0|https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/howToUse"
msgid "Link the actual Quantity, retain its original magnitude through math:quantityValue, keep its inherited actual dimension and require its frame to agree with this region’s actual coordinate frame."
msgstr "连接实际 Quantity，通过 math:quantityValue 保留原始数值，保留其继承的实际维度，并要求其参考系与此区域实际的坐标参考系一致。"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionX1|http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label"
msgid "source region x1"
msgstr "来源区域 x1"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/sourceRegionX1|http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"
msgid "The existing math:Quantity retaining the original numeric value supplied in the x1 coordinate slot of this SourceRegion."
msgstr "保留此 SourceRegion 的 x1 坐标槽中来源提供的原始数值的现有 math:Quantity。"

